cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these results or this code, please cite it as below."
title: "debruijn-newman-large-sieve: three results on the large sieve with prime moduli and the de Bruijn-Newman constant"
abstract: >-
  (1) The log log Q factor in Wolke's large sieve inequality with prime moduli is necessary, answering
  a question of Iwaniec (2022). (2) The de Bruijn-Newman constant is unbounded on the family of Dirichlet
  series sharing the functional equation of L(s, chi_-7). (3) The de Bruijn-Newman constant of the
  Davenport-Heilbronn function exceeds 0.23 (certified); an upper bound of 0.58 is conditional on
  error-term lemmas that are only sketched. Unrefereed; produced by an autonomous multi-agent research
  system, with interval-arithmetic certificates and a Lean 4 formalisation of the finite core of (1).
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Nozero Day"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - large sieve
  - prime moduli
  - de Bruijn-Newman constant
  - Davenport-Heilbronn function
  - Lean 4
